---
description: Deploy OpenCode app UI fixes into the installed desktop app for local testing
alwaysApply: true
---

For this repo, when app UI changes are meant to be tested through the installed desktop executable, finish by deploying the built renderer change into `C:\Users\crisc\AppData\Local\Programs\@opencode-aidesktop\resources\app.asar` so `C:\Users\crisc\AppData\Local\Programs\@opencode-aidesktop\OpenCode.exe` picks it up on the next launch.

## Standard: always a full ASAR redeploy with a **prod** desktop build

Always perform a **complete** redeploy — never partial same-length in-place string patches, and **never** copy `packages/app/dist` directly into the ASAR.

A dev-channel build (`OPENCODE_CHANNEL` unset or `dev`) bakes `VITE_OPENCODE_CHANNEL !== "prod"` into the renderer, which enables `newLayoutDesigns` by default and routes through different layout/storage paths. Deploying that into the installed production app makes existing sessions and project state appear to vanish.

### Build + deploy workflow

```powershell
# 1. Production desktop build (renderer + main + preload)
cd packages/desktop
$env:OPENCODE_CHANNEL = "prod"
bun run build

# 2. Full ASAR redeploy (script refuses to run without OPENCODE_CHANNEL=prod|latest)
cd ../opencode
$env:OPENCODE_CHANNEL = "prod"
bun run deploy-asar.ts
```

`deploy-asar.ts`:

1. Refuses to run unless `OPENCODE_CHANNEL` is `prod` or `latest`.
2. Makes a timestamped `app.asar.bak-*` backup of the current archive.
3. Extracts the live ASAR via `@electron/asar`.
4. Replaces `out/{main,preload,renderer}` inside the ASAR with `packages/desktop/out/{main,preload,renderer}`.
5. Repacks the ASAR so integrity hashes are recomputed.
6. Verifies marker strings (including prod channel) in the new archive; on failure restores the backup.

Hard constraints:

- Create the timestamped `app.asar.bak-*` backup before touching the archive.
- Do NOT restart the app or the server process — the next launch of `OpenCode.exe` picks up the new ASAR.
- If sessions disappear after a deploy, the most likely cause is a dev-channel build; rebuild with `OPENCODE_CHANNEL=prod` and redeploy.
